==Swedish==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɑːˌɡɔm/|lang=sv}} {{audio|sv-lagom.ogg|Audio}}

===Etymology 1===
Since 1675, [[plural]] [[dative]] form of ''[[lag]]'' "law" meaning "just, right, appropriate".

====Adverb====
{{sv-adv|mermest}}

# (just) right, [[fitting]], neither too much nor too little
#: ''Vi har skaffat en '''lagom''' dyr bil.''
#:: "We’ve bought a car that’s just the right price."

===Etymology 2===
Since 1637.

====Adjective====
{{infl|sv|adjective}}

# (just) right, [[fitting]], neither too much nor too little
#: ''Den här lägenheten är precis '''lagom''' för min dotter.''
#:: "This apartment is just right for my daughter."

